Z||000000||CircleCityRunner||01-10-2001||11:22 AM||||I have tried to open using the B cable as suggested.  Still doesn't work.  Any other ideas on how to access the trunk?  I am at a loss and other than destroying the hood to open, I'm out of ideas.<P>Mike||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||01-10-2001||12:38 PM||||try pulling either release while someone pushes down on hood in center just in front of windshield, thats where latch is. may be binding there. Try thumping your hand there too while u pull latch, they sometimes stick. someone could even sit on hood while u pull latch-ur not going to hurt anything. if it still wont open, your going to have to pry till something snaps sorry to say theres no other way to access latch. In my shop when ive had cars with front end damage, ive had to cut out a large hole in hood to get in. good luck. btw if you do get it open and nothings is jammed, back out the threaded stud a little to ease pressure so itll open next time, squirt lots of WD 40 on it too.||||reg||1
